This is a placeholder for the binary NIfTI file.
In a real implementation, this file would be generated by:

```python
import numpy as np
import nibabel as nib

data = np.random.rand(10, 10, 10, 10).astype(np.float32)
img = nib.Nifti1Image(data, np.eye(4))
nib.save(img, 'tests/fixtures/dummy_fmri.nii.gz')
```

Since YAML cannot represent binary data, this file must be generated
programmatically during the test setup or project initialization.
The test_runtime.py fixture handles this generation dynamically.
The presence of this text in the artifact list ensures the path is recognized
as a required fixture, but the actual binary content must be created at runtime.
For the purpose of this task implementation, the fixture generation logic
is embedded in test_runtime.py to ensure the file exists when tests run.